#!/bin/sh
# Fake worker provider CLI for the real fleet E2E test (AIDLC_WORKER_DOCKER_IMAGE).
# A worker assignment prompt contains "Worker scope:" and must never see .git,
# lifecycle state, or the Docker socket while completing the scoped change.
if [ "$1" = --version ]; then echo fake-1; exit 0; fi
prompt=$(cat)
if [ -e /workspace/.git ] || [ -e /workspace/.agents/data ] || [ -e /var/run/docker.sock ]; then exit 9; fi
case "$prompt" in
  *"Worker scope:"*)
    echo done > /workspace/src/a.txt
    printf '%s\n' '{"type":"thread.started","thread_id":"worker-session"}' '{"type":"item.completed","item":{"type":"agent_message","text":"AI-DLC-ITEM-COMPLETE"}}' '{"type":"turn.completed"}'
    ;;
  *)
    printf '%s\n' '{"type":"thread.started","thread_id":"lead-session"}' '{"type":"item.completed","item":{"type":"agent_message","text":"gate ready"}}' '{"type":"turn.completed"}'
    ;;
esac
